$ whycant -u alice write /srv/shared.log

✗ alice (uid 1000) cannot write /srv/shared.log

  /                 drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /srv              drwxr-xr-x  root:root    ✓ traverse
  /srv/shared.log   -rw-r--rw-  root:deploy  ✗ write   ← blocked here

Why
  alice is not the owner (root) but is in group "deploy",
  so the group permissions apply: r--. Writing to a file needs w.
  The other permissions (rw-) would allow it, but they never apply to members
  of the file's group.

Fixes (safest first)
  1. Grant write access only to alice via ACL:
       sudo setfacl -m u:alice:w /srv/shared.log
  2. Give group "deploy" the missing w permission (this affects every member of deploy):
       sudo chmod g+w /srv/shared.log
